1
00:00:00,480 --> 00:00:08,500
From VOA Learning English, this is the Health & Lifestyle report.

2
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:18,320
New guidelines have been issued in the United States for preventing stroke – the nation’s 4th biggest killer.

3
00:00:18,180 --> 00:00:32,940
The U.S. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) says that in 2023, stroke was the fourth leading cause of death in the United States.

4
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:40,440
An estimated half a million people suffer strokes in the U.S. each year.

5
00:00:39,940 --> 00:00:57,620
But the CDC notes that up to 80 percent of strokes could be prevented with better nutrition and exercise, along with improved risk identification.

6
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:09,810
A stroke happens when blood flow to part of the brain is blocked or if a blood vessel in the brain breaks open, or bursts.

7
00:01:09,740 --> 00:01:14,820
The event keeps oxygen from getting to the brain.

8
00:01:14,440 --> 00:01:21,620
This can result in the person having difficulty thinking, talking and walking.

9
00:01:21,520 --> 00:01:25,360
In some cases, a stroke can even cause death.

10
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:31,620
Stroke is a major health problem across the world.

11
00:01:31,520 --> 00:01:43,500
On its website, the World Stroke Organization says the condition is a leading cause of death and disability worldwide.

12
00:01:43,180 --> 00:01:48,830
Over 100 million people worldwide have suffered a stroke.

13
00:01:48,740 --> 00:01:59,460
It is estimated that 25 percent of adults over 25 will have a stroke during their lifetime.

14
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:06,200
The new guidelines on stroke prevention came from the American Stroke Association.

15
00:02:06,050 --> 00:02:10,900
They are the first to be issued in 10 years.

16
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:23,280
The advice includes suggestions for people and doctors and are based on improved information about who has strokes and why.

17
00:02:22,680 --> 00:02:30,380
The guidelines also include new drugs that can help reduce risk.

18
00:02:29,940 --> 00:02:43,240
Health researchers say the best way to reduce the risk of stroke is the same as reducing risks for many other conditions.

19
00:02:43,020 --> 00:02:52,400
These include eating a healthy diet, moving the body often and not smoking.

20
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:59,400
Here is what to know about stroke and the newly issued guidelines:

21
00:02:58,900 --> 00:03:05,460
Experts say eating healthy can help control possible stroke risks.

22
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:19,160
The goal is to prevent or reduce high cholesterol, high blood sugar and obesity, the condition of being extremely overweight.

23
00:03:19,020 --> 00:03:24,800
The advice urges people to choose foods in the so-called Mediterranean diet.

24
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:32,580
These include fruits, vegetables, whole grains and olive oil.

25
00:03:32,220 --> 00:03:39,800
Eating these foods can help keep cholesterol levels down.

26
00:03:39,580 --> 00:03:44,660
Red meat should be limited, along with saturated fats.

27
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:54,329
Additional protein can come from beans, nuts, poultry and seafood.

28
00:03:54,000 --> 00:04:00,650
Highly processed foods and drinks with a lot of added sugar should also be avoided.

29
00:04:00,100 --> 00:04:15,640
Getting up and walking around for at least 10 minutes a day can greatly reduce a person’s stroke risk, said Dr. Cheryl Bushnell.

30
00:04:15,220 --> 00:04:24,100
She is a neurologist at Wake Forest University School of Medicine in North Carolina.

31
00:04:23,480 --> 00:04:29,720
Bushnell was part of the group that came up with the new guidelines.

32
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:37,720
She said regular exercise can help reduce blood pressure, a major risk factor for stroke.

33
00:04:37,160 --> 00:04:44,080
However, health experts say more movement is better.

34
00:04:43,890 --> 00:04:59,520
The stroke association suggests at least 150 minutes of moderate aerobic or 75 minutes of vigorous exercise activity every week.

35
00:04:59,240 --> 00:05:06,560
Such exercise could include going to the gym, taking a walk or running.

36
00:05:06,180 --> 00:05:15,400
People can also use exercise machines at home, dance or play a sport.

37
00:05:15,250 --> 00:05:23,710
The guidelines include a new group of drugs that have been proven to help people lose weight.

38
00:05:23,640 --> 00:05:35,560
The drugs – designed for people with obesity or diabetes – had not been approved when past guidelines were issued.

39
00:05:35,260 --> 00:05:44,520
But the advice now suggests doctors consider these drugs for patients at risk for stroke.

40
00:05:44,320 --> 00:05:54,820
These include versions sold under the names Ozempic, Wegovy, Mounjaro, and Zepbound.

41
00:05:54,700 --> 00:06:04,080
The new guidelines also help doctors identify people who might be at higher risk for stroke.

42
00:06:03,960 --> 00:06:13,620
For the first time, the advice suggests doctors screen patients for other risk factors.

43
00:06:13,300 --> 00:06:24,700
They could include gender or non-medical factors such as economic issues or the availability of quality health care.

44
00:06:24,580 --> 00:06:35,640
The new guidelines also suggest that doctors screen for conditions that may increase a woman’s risk for stroke.

45
00:06:35,200 --> 00:06:43,640
These could include high blood pressure during pregnancy or early menopause.

46
00:06:43,160 --> 00:06:54,980
Three of the most common stroke signs include face weakness, arm weakness and difficulty speaking.

47
00:06:54,520 --> 00:07:00,980
Also, time is important when a person suffers a stroke.

48
00:07:00,720 --> 00:07:10,200
Brain damage can happen quickly, but it can be limited if a stroke is treated quickly.

49
00:07:09,860 --> 00:07:26,640
Stroke experts have created an acronym to help people remember: FAST -- F for face, A for arm, S for speech, and T for time.

50
00:07:26,520 --> 00:07:36,220
If you think you or a loved one may be having a stroke, call the emergency response number in your area immediately.

51
00:07:36,100 --> 00:07:39,870
And that’s the Health & Lifestyle report.

52
00:07:39,660 --> 00:07:41,640
I’m Anna Matteo.

53
00:07:41,480 --> 00:07:43,500
And I’m Bryan Lynn.
